From c8beec279cfa63fd98eefdf04a063eb9040f4a9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartheek Palla <kartheek@sanketika.in>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:50:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(oid4vc-service): the over-disclosure check was never
 reached in practice
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

extractCredentials() produced disclosedNames and the matcher consumed it, but
the one place that connects them — the multi-credential keyed vp_token branch,
which is the path every SD-JWT presentation in this deployment takes — built
its `presented` entry without it. So the check silently did nothing against a
live stack while all eight unit tests passed, because each of them hands the
matcher a fixture written by hand.

Three tests now drive the matcher from a real SD-JWT built the way a wallet
builds one, through the actual extractCredentials(), with no fixture in the
middle. That is the shape of test that would have caught this.

Also fixes the cross-issuer refusal message for a vct-only request. Each
instance normalises a RELATIVE schema vct against its own PUBLIC_URL, so the
school renders the college's type as `<host>/school/vct/<slug>` while the
wallet asks for `<host>/college/vct/<slug>`; comparing whole vcts across
instances is therefore always false, and the refusal fell back to "could not
determine the credential type" — which sends an operator looking for a schema
that is present and simply belongs to somebody else. Compared on the type slug
via a new vctSlug() helper, with the reason for it written down where the next
person will hit it.
